Ok, here is the R code of the model I am building.
I want to be able to estimate hiv prevalence. I have the total number of persons tested and numbers who are positive for only 8 counties while for 32 others I only have the covariates. My goal is to be able to predict for the 32 where no data was collected.

hiv_data$HIV_postives<-as.integer(hiv_data$HIV_postives)
hiv_data$Total_tested<-as.integer(hiv_data$Total_tested)

hiv_data$prev<-hiv_data$HIV_postives/hiv_data$Total_tested # Observed prevalence

## covariates.  I have total population data and tota number of persons living with HIV as covariates and they are continuous variables.

hiv_data$PLHIV_scaled <- scale(hiv_data$PLHIV)
hiv_data$population_scaled <- scale(hiv_data$population)

# 4. Model (non-spatial)
formula <- prev ~ 1+PLHIV_scaled+population_scaled  + f(county_id, model = "iid", hyper = list(prec = list(prior = "pc.prec", param = c(1, 0.01))))

# 5. Fit model
result <- inla(formula, family = "binomial", Ntrials = Total_tested, data = hiv_data)

